  "projectUrl": "https://pwfauth.com/",
  "published": "2026-10-01T17:10:29.453Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- A wrong system clock now repairs itself. The server's refusal for a clock more than 5 minutes off carries its own time (reason CLOCK_SKEW, server_time); the client shifts its timestamps by the difference and sends the request once more, so sign-in and the heartbeat keep working on a PC whose date or time is wrong. Opt out with PwfClientOptions.AutoCorrectClock = false (the 1.1 behaviour).\n- New CryptoEnvelope.ClockOffsetSeconds: the shift in use, for callers of PostEnvelopeAsync or of the envelope directly.\n- Every request sends User-Agent: PWFAuth-dotnet/1.2.0 (+https://pwfauth.com).\nFull history: https://github.com/pwfauth/pwfauth-dotnet/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
